# Restart the local app after updates

After changing anything the running app loads (`app/`, the Docker image, or compose config), restart it on this machine before the user tests and before any commit.

From the repo root:

```powershell
docker compose restart rag
```

`docker compose up -d` does not reload Python in an already-running container. The page HTML is read on each request. Python modules are imported at startup, so a `.py` change is invisible until this restart.

Before restarting, check `http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/status`. If `ingest.running` is true, do not restart. Never run `docker compose down -v`. That deletes the pgvector index.

After the restart, confirm the app is up. Leave committing until the user asks.
